For a system of two linear equations in two variables, the condition for a unique solution (intersecting lines) is that the slopes of the lines are not equal. The slope of $a_1x + b_1y = c_1$ is $-a_1/b_1$ and the slope of $a_2x + b_2y = c_2$ is $-a_2/b_2$. Setting these not equal: $-a_1/b_1 
eq -a_2/b_2 \implies  rac{a_1}{b_1} 
eq  rac{a_2}{b_2} \implies  rac{a_1}{a_2} 
eq  rac{b_1}{b_2}$. This represents the condition for a unique (one) solution.
